<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="63533" href="schedule/2020/spring/UP/494/63533.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2020" href="schedule/2020.xml">2020</calendarYear><term id="120201" href="schedule/2020/spring.xml">Spring 2020</term><subject id="UP" href="schedule/2020/spring/UP.xml">Urban and Regional Planning</subject><course id="494" href="schedule/2020/spring/UP/494.xml">Special Topics in Planning</course></parents><sectionNumber>AG </sectionNumber><sectionTitle>Neighborhood Analysis</sectionTitle><creditHours>4 hours</creditHours><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>Survey of quantitative and qualitative methods for analyzing demographic, economic, physical, and social conditions at the neighborhood and local government scale. Analytical techniques cover the description of past and present conditions, and the projection of future trends. Treatment of how analysis guides local deliberative processes and decision-making, and training in methods for engaging public, government, and private stakeholders in conversations regarding scenarios derived from analysis.</sectionText><partOfTerm>1</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>UNKNOWN</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2020-01-21Z</startDate><endDate>2020-05-06Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="LEC">Lecture</type><start>02:00 PM</start><end>03:20 PM</end><daysOfTheWeek>TR     </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>19</roomNumber><buildingName>Temple Hoyne Buell Hall</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Balachandran" firstName="S">Balachandran, S</instructor><instructor lastName="Greenlee" firstName="A">Greenlee, A</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>